course: dictionary
lesson: 1166
title: A word for people from Britain
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Briton is a noun, and it names a person. A Briton is a person from Britain, a British citizen. The plural is Britons, for more than one person. «Helen Sharman became the first Briton in space in 1991.» Here Briton means one person from Britain. It is a formal word, so you will meet it in serious writing and the news.
explain: The word also has a history meaning. The Ancient Britons were the Celtic people who lived in Britain before and during the time of the Romans. To tell which meaning is meant, check the context. «Britain was settled over time by Celtic Britons, Romans, Anglo-Saxons, Vikings and Normans» is about the past, so Britons means the ancient peoples.
explain: «Britons are reported to drink about 100 million cups a day» is about people today, so Britons means people from Britain now. Ask yourself: is this sentence about the past or about people today? The answer tells you which meaning to use.
fact: Briton means a person from Britain, and it is a noun.
fact: The plural is Britons: one Briton, but two or more Britons.
fact: Briton is a formal word, so it is often used in news and official writing.
fact: The Ancient Britons were the Celtic people who lived in Britain before and during the time of the Romans.
fact: In history lessons, the Ancient Britons fought the Romans, and their famous queen was Boudicca.
exercise: «Helen Sharman became the first Briton in space in 1991.» What is a Briton? | A type of space rocket | A planet far away | A kind of tea | *A person from Britain
exercise: «Britons are reported to drink about 100 million cups a day.» Who does Britons refer to here? | *People from Britain today | The Ancient Britons who fought the Romans | Chinese tea farmers | Robert Fortune
exercise: Which is the plural of Briton? | Briton's | Brittons | *Britons | Britain
test: «Britain was settled over time by Celtic Britons, Romans, Anglo-Saxons, Vikings and Normans.» In this sentence, Britons means | *The Celtic people who lived in Britain long ago | Modern-day people from Britain | Romans who came to Britain | Vikings with ships
test: Which sentence uses Briton to mean one person from Britain today? | The Ancient Britons fought the Romans. | *Helen Sharman was the first Briton in space. | Tea came from China.
exam: In «only about 1 percent of Britons now work on the land», what does Britons mean? | *People from Britain today | Farmers from China | Ancient Celtic people | Roman soldiers
